From ba6a058cff179cd9e8d970ec0253e2cf09fb34e5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 20:51:57 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] fix(kanban): governor/pool gates park as an internal
 'resource' wait that resumes on its probe, never escalates, and backs off on
 repeats

A bb-gate governor hold ('memory pressure warn; Claude pool at 87%') parked undeclared, so core inferred {kind: external, inferred: true, ref: <host launch command>} and the 3rd park escalated into an Unstick card (bb t_01a18aa302529d91 / t_01a19f5cca30ed12). awaiting kind='resource' needs a wake_check, keys its premise on the gate (not the reading), never raises RepeatedPark, and a repeat park doubles check_every (cap 1h) with the gate named in the reason. Genuine external premises still escalate on the 3rd park.
